/-
Mathathon Round 1, Problem 59: official Lean statement, prepared by AI. It may contain errors.

Written by AI for Mathathon; not taken from an existing formalization.
It states Theorem 1.1 of the OpenAI preprint "Bloch's conjecture for surfaces with p_g = 0"
(September 2026), the case of Bloch's conjecture that the preprint proves: if `S` is a smooth
connected projective complex surface with `p_g(S) = q(S) = 0`, then the degree map
`CH₀(S) → ℤ` is an isomorphism, with integral coefficients. The degree map is onto (a closed point
has degree one), so the statement says that every zero-cycle of degree zero is rationally
equivalent to zero.
Modelling choices:
* `S` comes with a morphism `p : S ⟶ Spec ℂ` that is proper and smooth of relative dimension 2,
  and `S` is connected. A smooth proper surface over a field is projective (Zariski), so "proper"
  is equivalent to "projective" here.
* `q(S) = h¹(S, 𝒪_S)` and, by Serre duality, `p_g(S) = h⁰(S, ω_S) = h²(S, 𝒪_S)`. The hypotheses
  say that `H¹(S, 𝒪_S)` and `H²(S, 𝒪_S)` vanish, where `H^n` is Mathlib's sheaf cohomology
  `Sheaf.H` (Ext groups in the category of abelian sheaves on the Zariski space of `S`) of the
  structure sheaf, viewed as a sheaf of abelian groups.
* Zero-cycles are Mathlib's algebraic cycles `AlgebraicCycle S ℤ` supported on closed points, with
  Mathlib's degree `AlgebraicCycle.degree`. As in Fulton, Intersection Theory, §§1.2–1.3, rational
  equivalence is generated by the push-forwards of the divisors `div f = ∑ ord_z(f) [z]` of nonzero
  rational functions `f` on integral closed curves `C` in `S`; `ord_z` is Mathlib's `Scheme.ord`,
  defined through lengths as in Fulton.
The case `q > 0` of Bloch's conjecture (Bloch–Kas–Lieberman, 1976) involves the Albanese variety,
which Mathlib does not have; it is not stated.
-/

import Mathlib

namespace Mathathon.P59

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

/-- The structure sheaf of a scheme `S`, viewed as a sheaf of abelian groups on the underlying
topological space of `S`. -/
noncomputable def structureSheafAb (S : Scheme.{u}) :
    Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u} :=
  (sheafCompose _ (forget₂ RingCat AddCommGrpCat)).obj S.ringCatSheaf

/-- The sheaf cohomology group `Hⁿ(S, 𝒪_S)`: the `n`-th Ext group, in the category of abelian
sheaves on `S`, from the constant sheaf `ℤ` to the structure sheaf (Mathlib's `Sheaf.H`). -/
noncomputable def structureSheafCohomology (S : Scheme.{u}) (n : ℕ) : Type u :=
  haveI : HasExt.{u} (Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u}) :=
    hasExt_of_enoughInjectives _
  Sheaf.H (structureSheafAb S) n

/-- The degree of a cycle on a scheme `S` that is quasi-compact over `Spec k`:
`∑ₓ [κ(x) : k] · D x` (Mathlib's `AlgebraicCycle.degree`). For a zero-cycle on a variety over an
algebraically closed field this is the sum of the coefficients. -/
noncomputable def degree {S : Scheme.{u}} {k : CommRingCat.{u}} (p : S ⟶ Spec k)
    [QuasiCompact p] (D : AlgebraicCycle S ℤ) : ℤ :=
  haveI : CompactSpace S := QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace p
  AlgebraicCycle.degree p D

/-- `D` is the divisor of a nonzero rational function on an integral curve in `S`, pushed forward
to `S`: there are a closed immersion `i : C ⟶ S` of an integral scheme `C` of dimension one and a
nonzero element `f` of the function field of `C` such that `D (i z) = ord_z(f)` for every point
`z` of `C` and `D` vanishes off the image of `i`. (`Scheme.ord f z` is the order of vanishing of
`f` at a point `z` of codimension one, here a closed point of `C`, and `0` at the generic point.) -/
def IsDivisorOnCurve (S : Scheme.{u}) (D : AlgebraicCycle S ℤ) : Prop :=
  ∃ (C : Scheme.{u}) (_ : IsIntegral C) (_ : IsLocallyNoetherian C) (i : C ⟶ S)
    (_ : IsClosedImmersion i) (f : C.functionField),
    topologicalKrullDim C = 1 ∧ f ≠ 0 ∧
    (∀ z : C, D (i.base z) = Scheme.ord f z) ∧ ∀ x : S, x ∉ Set.range i.base → D x = 0

/-- The cycles rationally equivalent to zero: the subgroup generated by the divisors of nonzero
rational functions on integral curves in `S`. -/
def rationallyTrivial (S : Scheme.{u}) : AddSubgroup (AlgebraicCycle S ℤ) :=
  AddSubgroup.closure {D | IsDivisorOnCurve S D}

/-- Bloch's conjecture for surfaces with `p_g = q = 0` (Theorem 1.1 of the OpenAI preprint): on a
smooth connected projective complex surface `S` with `H¹(S, 𝒪_S) = H²(S, 𝒪_S) = 0`, every
zero-cycle of degree zero is rationally equivalent to zero, that is, `deg : CH₀(S) → ℤ` is
injective (hence an isomorphism). -/
theorem bloch_pg_eq_q_eq_zero (S : Scheme.{0}) (p : S ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of ℂ))
    [IsProper p] [SmoothOfRelativeDimension 2 p] [ConnectedSpace S]
    (hq : Subsingleton (structureSheafCohomology S 1))
    (hpg : Subsingleton (structureSheafCohomology S 2))
    (D : AlgebraicCycle S ℤ) (hD : ∀ x, D x ≠ 0 → IsClosed ({x} : Set S))
    (hdeg : degree p D = 0) :
    D ∈ rationallyTrivial S := by
  sorry

end Mathathon.P59
